@@ -95,3 +95,21 @@ When it does happen, you get a structured envelope rather than a raw `TypeError`
 
 Both messages tell the model the questions were never shown and to ask them as plain chat
 text instead of treating the failure as a decline.
+
+## Opt-in companion replies
+
+With `companionReplies: true`, the actual terminal overlay can also be answered through
+the [public event API](./companion-replies.md). Requests are published only for
+`ctx.mode === "tui"`, after successful component construction/completion binding and
+Pi's public `onHandle` notification that the overlay is shown. Terminal answers and
+validated external answers share the existing `done` callback and are arbitrated once.
+The callback dismisses the overlay; no editor or `ctx.ui` replacement is used.
+RPC/default-off behavior and legacy notification timing/payloads are unchanged.
+
+The tool abort signal and public `session_shutdown` cancel an opted-in invocation via
+the existing cancellation envelope, remove its reply listener, and suppress any pending
+publication. Cancellation during lazy loading skips UI creation; cancellation after construction
+but before overlay readiness is delivered only after mounting (Pi's callback removes
+that overlay). Every published invocation emits one
+closure, including custom-UI errors; abrupt process death cannot emit a closure.
+Client unsubscription/disconnect has no effect on terminal completion.
