@@ -0,0 +1,136 @@
+# Companion reply API (v1)
+
+This package-specific public interface answers the **same** `ask_user_question` TUI
+invocation. It is not Pi-wide dialog middleware. No second tool, renderer, network
+server, broker, auth layer or settings editor is added.
+
+## Enable and subscribe
+
+In the read-only [config file](configuration.md), explicitly set:
+
+```json
+{ "companionReplies": true }
+```
+
+Restart/reload Pi. Default is off; only boolean `true` enables the interface.
+This authorizes trusted in-process subscribers to see full questions, descriptions
+and previews and submit answers. The event bus is not an authentication boundary.
+A companion must secure its own transport and not forward sensitive content indiscriminately.
+
+Imports are available from the root and `/events` package exports. All payloads are
+JSON-safe; channels are versioned, with the existing append-only stability policy.
+
+| Export | Channel | Direction |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `ASK_USER_REQUEST_EVENT` | `rpiv:ask-user:request.v1` | package → client |
+| `ASK_USER_REPLY_EVENT` | `rpiv:ask-user:reply.v1` | client → package |
+| `ASK_USER_REPLY_OUTCOME_EVENT` | `rpiv:ask-user:reply-outcome.v1` | package → client |
+| `ASK_USER_CLOSED_EVENT` | `rpiv:ask-user:closed.v1` | package → client |
+
+```ts
+import {
+  ASK_USER_REQUEST_EVENT, ASK_USER_REPLY_EVENT,
+  ASK_USER_REPLY_OUTCOME_EVENT, ASK_USER_CLOSED_EVENT,
+  type AskUserRequestEventPayload, type AskUserReplyEventPayload,
+} from "@juicesharp/rpiv-ask-user-question/events";
+
+const unsubscribe = pi.events.on(ASK_USER_REQUEST_EVENT, (request: AskUserRequestEventPayload) => {
+  // Show request.questions; keep request.invocationId for the user's explicit reply.
+});
+// On an explicit user selection, not automatically on request:
+const reply: AskUserReplyEventPayload = {
+  invocationId: pending.invocationId, replyId: clientRequestId,
+  cancelled: false,
+  answers: [{ questionIndex: 0, kind: "option", answer: pending.questions[0].options[0].label }],
+};
+pi.events.emit(ASK_USER_REPLY_EVENT, reply);
+// Subscribe to outcome and closure before sending; a reply may complete synchronously.
+// unsubscribe() simply detaches the observer; the terminal stays usable.
+```
+
+## Request and disclosure timing
+
+`AskUserRequestEventPayload` contains an opaque, fresh `invocationId` and ordered
+`questions[]`: `{ question, header, multiSelect, options[] }`, with options
+`{ label, description, preview? }`. These are full normalized authored strings
+(CRLF → LF; lone CR removed), not TUI sentinel rows or abbreviated previews.
+`multiSelect` is always boolean. The ID is not a tool-call ID or a durable session ID.
+
+One request is emitted only if enabled, `ctx.mode === "tui"`, the actual existing
+component was successfully constructed with its completion callback bound, and
+`ui.custom` invoked `onHandle` after showing the overlay. Component construction
+alone, `hasUI`, validation, RPC/unknown hosts and unrendered custom calls are not
+sufficient. A pending abort/shutdown suppresses publication. The legacy prompt and
+blocked events keep their existing behavior, including default-off and RPC paths.
+
+No replay/snapshot service exists. Subscribe before invocation. Reconnection after
+missing a request does not acquire a handle; the terminal remains authoritative.
+
+## Reply validation
+
+`AskUserReplyEventPayload` contains:
+
+- `invocationId`: exactly the active request's ID.
+- `replyId`: non-empty client correlation string, at most 128 UTF-16 code units.
+- `cancelled`: boolean.
+- `answers`: up to one entry per authored question, unique integer `questionIndex`
+  in the zero-based request range; partial submission and empty arrays are allowed.
+- Optional `globalNote`: string.
+
+Each answer has optional string `notes` and one variant:
+
+- `{ questionIndex, kind: "option", answer: string }`: single-select only, exact
+  authored option label (case/whitespace sensitive).
+- `{ questionIndex, kind: "custom", answer: string | null }`: either question mode,
+  matching the existing typed-answer result semantics (including empty/null values).
+- `{ questionIndex, kind: "multi", answer: null, selected: string[] }`: multi-select
+  only; unique exact authored labels, at most the number of authored options.
+  Empty selection is allowed. Selection order is retained.
+
+`ASK_USER_REPLY_MAX_BYTES` is 65,536 bytes for the complete JSON-serialized reply
+(UTF-8); `ASK_USER_REPLY_MAX_TEXT_LENGTH` is 8,192 UTF-16 code units per custom text,
+per-question note and global note. Oversized/unserializable replies are rejected.
+Unknown fields are tolerated but count toward the byte limit. They are not echoed:
+question text and selected preview are reconstructed exclusively from owner-authored
+normalized data. Whitespace-only notes are omitted; otherwise their original text
+is retained. The existing result formatter decides answered-vs-declined prose for
+empty/partial submissions, note-only submissions and cancellation. No tool schema,
+name, result field or model-facing error code is added.
+
+## Outcome, closure and races
+
+An active, correlatable invalid reply emits
+`{ invocationId, replyId, accepted: false, reason: "invalid_reply" }` and leaves the
+terminal and listener active. A validated winning reply emits
+`{ invocationId, replyId, accepted: true }`, then closure. Acceptance acknowledges
+only this live completion callback, **not native tool dispatch or durable persistence**.
+
+Closure is `{ invocationId, reason }`, exactly once per published invocation:
+`terminal`, `external`, `aborted`, `shutdown`, or `ended` (other/custom-UI exit).
+Discard that pending UI on closure. No final answer payload is broadcast. Terminal
+and external contenders use one invocation-owned once-only arbiter around the
+existing public `done`. The first completion wins; reentrant/duplicate contenders
+cannot change the result. External-first dismisses the terminal overlay; terminal-
+first closes the external pending request.
+
+Per-invocation reply listeners are removed at completion/error/abort/shutdown.
+Unknown, closed and inactive IDs are **ignored without acknowledgement**, as are
+uncorrelatable replies (missing/invalid `replyId`). There is no tombstone registry,
+permanent reply listener, retry cache or exactly-once transport guarantee. Do not
+blindly replay uncertain replies after reconnecting; a late attempt cannot alter
+another invocation. A captured handler already in dispatch also guards against
+completion. Client departure does not cancel the questionnaire.
+
+Abort uses the tool's supported signal; orderly reload/session replacement/process
+shutdown uses public `session_shutdown`. Both return the existing cancellation
+shape for opted-in invocations. Abrupt death cannot publish closure; clients must
+also treat owner disconnection as loss of their pending capability.
+
+## Checked scope
+
+Source tests use locked Pi 0.80.6 dependencies. The isolated source-loaded PTY probe
+under the parent project's `probes/run-questionnaire-replies.py` runs the installed
+Pi 0.99.2 TUI with no provider/model calls: external-first, terminal-first, invalid
+and late replies, client departure, and default-off. It captures the public tool
+definition and invokes it directly; it does **not** prove native model dispatch,
+transcript persistence, browser transport/security or general Pi version compatibility.
